36,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
37,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's exactly as I suspected. The bins are being emptied daily because people are eating at their desks, and the keyboards are filthy. The ""break room"" isn't even being used for its intended purpose.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The outside hire costs are... actually quite high. We've spent 68,000 yen on small bookings. And the fit-out quotes are 141,000 for a screen setup or 96,000 for a kitchen area. It's a lot of money.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It's not fair at all! Only two people are using the room almost all the time, while everyone else barely gets in there. It's like a first-come, first-served race!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a poignant reminder that we are drifting apart. Our conversations have shrunk to the space by the printer, and our walls are too thin to protect our privacy. We are strangers in a shared home.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The facilities logs show a clear pattern of maintenance burden in equipment rooms, while the walk for a hot lunch is a significant time sink for most of us every day.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, your ""poignant reminder"" is just a fancy way of saying the room is a mess. If the walls are too thin, it's because the noise from the filth and chaos is leaking out.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree that the costs are worrying. If we keep paying for outside rooms, it just adds up. But the fit-out quotes are also quite expensive... I'm not sure we can afford both.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, maybe we can save money if we stop paying for outside rooms and just fix our own! But we have to make sure the room isn't just for the people who get there first.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Shion, cleanliness is a matter of habit, but connection is a matter of the soul. If we only fix the bins and ignore the silence between us, we have merely cleaned a void.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, if we spend on a fit-out, we must ensure it doesn't create more upkeep. @Rin, the usage gap is concerning, but we should consider if the room's current layout is what's driving people away.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, the layout isn't the problem; the behavior is. People are treating the office like a cafeteria, and the break room is just a noise leak. We need a solution that actually separates the mess from the work.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried that if we don't pick a clear purpose, we'll just keep paying those outside hire fees. But spending over a hundred thousand yen on a fit-out feels like a huge risk. I don't want to be responsible for a mistake.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shion, it's not just about the mess! I found out that some people are barely using the room because others just hog it. If we don't have a real plan, the same things will just happen again!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Servas,,"My dear friends, let us not let the fear of cost or the frustration of habits blind us. We must create a sanctuary where we can speak honestly and rediscover one another's company.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, a sanctuary requires maintenance. If we create a space that demands constant cleaning or long commutes for food, the ""spirit"" will be crushed by the sheer amount of wasted time and labor.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, you're finally speaking my language. Logic over sentiment. If we don't address the fact that people are eating at their desks and making a mess, any ""sanctuary"" will just be a glorified trash can.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
54,2,4,pass,Shion,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
55,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should be careful. If we spend a lot on a fit-out but it doesn't solve the problem, we'll just be losing money in two different ways. I'm really worried about the budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
56,2,4,pass,Daisuke,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
57,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just don't want us to keep fighting or feeling bad because some people take over the room! We need a rule that makes it fair, or it doesn't matter how much we spend on it!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Servas,,"True fairness is not found in a set of rules, but in a space that invites us to be vulnerable and open. Let us build a bridge back to one another.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"We are talking about bridges and souls, but we are ignoring the fact that we lose nearly two hours a week just walking for lunch. Any solution must reduce this wasted time and labor.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
60,2,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
