66,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is a disaster waiting to happen. We already have crumbs in the keyboards; giving people a kitchen will just move the mess and the noise closer to our desks. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Option A too, because of the cost and the mess. But Option B would stop those outside hire fees we've been paying. I think B is the safest for the budget.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option B sounds great! If we have a shared calendar, then nobody can just hog the room by getting there first. It makes it fair for everyone to have a turn!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Servas,,"While a calendar brings order, we must ask if it also brings a wall. A room for ""bookings"" may stop the hogging, but will it invite the spontaneous, heartfelt conversations we so desperately lack?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is a trap. ""Maintained by whoever uses them"" is a recipe for unpaid labor and inevitable decay. Option B is logical for the budget, but Option C minimizes the maintenance burden entirely.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, your ""spontaneous conversations"" are exactly what I hear through the wall while I'm trying to work. Option C is the only choice that actually solves the noise pollution and the chaos.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree that noise is a problem, but if we choose Option C, we'll still be paying for those outside rooms. I'm really worried about that monthly cost continuing. Option B seems like the only way to stop it.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, you're right! If we pick B, we save money and everyone gets a fair chance to use it. Option C sounds a bit lonely, and I don't want us to just sit in silence!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you speak a truth that resonates. Silence can be a sanctuary, but it can also be a shroud. If we choose a path that isolates us further, we may find ourselves in a very clean room, yet still entirely alone.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, isolation is preferable to a system that fails. @Daisuke, while B saves on hire fees, it introduces the labor of managing a calendar and the noise of meetings. C is the most sustainable for our time.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, exactly. Sustainability isn't just about money; it's about mental bandwidth. Option B just replaces one kind of noise with another. Option C is the only logical way to reclaim our focus and peace.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I understand that, but the money is already leaving our accounts every month. If we don't have a place for meetings, we'll just keep paying those invoices. I'm too scared to ignore the budget.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but if we pick C, we're just ignoring the problem of people hogging the space! A calendar in Option B is like a magic shield that stops the unfairness. I'm voting for B!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Servas,,"My dear Rin, a shield can protect us, but it can also keep us apart. If we only meet by appointment, we lose the chance to truly see one another. We need a place for the difficult, honest words.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, a calendar is just another administrative task that someone will eventually be stuck managing. @Daisuke, the budget is a concern, but the cost of our time and mental energy is higher. I'm leaning toward C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, your fear of the budget is blinding you to the cost of our productivity. @Rin, ""fairness"" isn't worth a room full of noise. I'm voting for Option C. It's the only logical choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I know you're right about the noise, but I can't stop thinking about those invoices. If we don't stop the outside hire, we're just wasting money. I'll vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm sticking with B! It's the only way to make sure everyone gets a turn and we stop wasting money. Let's make it fair and organized! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Servas,,"We must not let the ledger be our only guide. If we choose a room of silence or a room of schedules, we risk remaining strangers. I vote for Option B, for it at least brings us together.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
85,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is a compromise that addresses the budget, but it doesn't solve the labor issue. However, Option A is out of the question. To avoid further chaos, I vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
